## Open from the 2026-10-07 lightcurve work (branch lightcurve-fixes)
- Position search: `--position "<ra> <dec>"` (opt-in, not the default), once radio_search2
  gains its `POS <ra> <dec>` mode (patch + note handed to radio_search2's maintainer; it
  runs on several machines and is updated in one go). Search with
  `radio_search2 POS ra dec BANDS ...`, skip name resolution, set source_ra/decl directly;
  carry it through CLI, GUI, harness and import.json.
- Lightcurve plot: epochs whose target lies beyond PB_RELIABLE_FWHMS (0.75 FWHM) are
  plotted like the others although their beam correction is uncertain by 2x or more --
  drop them or give them a distinct marker (lightcurve_plot.py; user to choose).
- First real case for the Airy vptable (below): the DDO52 fields (AH0927, AL0091, AS0622)
  have a 456 mJy NVSS source 58' out, beyond the beam model and unmodelled; it probably
  limits the 2008-07 D-config epoch (8.8 mJy limit).
- resolve_source's NED fallback (a name SIMBAD lacks) is untested: NED timed out all day.
- setjy flux-scale bug (fixed in cba6f69): every output made before it is low by the
  flux calibrator's flux; old sweeps need re-running. Tell Dom.
- No absolute thermal-noise QA: importvla weights and visibility scatter both come out
  ~15-20x below the image noise for good and bad runs alike.
- Spectral-line data is only channel-averaged (to MAX_IMAGING_CHANNELS); nothing else in
  the pipeline knows about line setups (narrow 2-6 MHz bands, HI programs).
- casaviewer: the PNG viewer can hang in imview(); reap_viewers() in the harness cleans
  up after a run, but a single interactive run still relies on _shutdown_casaviewer().

## P band (experimental, branch p-band-experimental): the first live sessions
P band runs attended only (decisions.require_attended; README "P band"). Nobody here has
reduced classic-VLA 90 cm data with this pipeline yet, so the first sessions are for
finding what breaks. Test data in data_archive/AD0308 (seg A, 1993-06-16, C config,
NGC 4565 field, IC 3599 46.7' out; 3C286 = 1328+307 as flux calibrator).
- AD0308 cannot be parsed as imported: its field/source names hold spaces ('NGC 4565_1'),
  which parse_listobs's fields/sources/scans regexes do not allow (parse_sources raises
  "could not convert string to float: 'any'"). Fix the parser first, or run on a copy of
  the MS with the spaces in FIELD/SOURCE NAME replaced. importvla also split the pointing
  into several fields ('NGC 4565_1', 'NGC 4565', and slew records labelled with the next
  source's name), and the pipeline images one field.
- RFI: what tfcrop flags at 327 MHz, per spw and baseline; whether the plotms review is
  enough to judge it, or rflag/extend and a per-channel look are needed.
- Bandpass: 1-channel continuum data have none to speak of; line-mode data (32 x 97.7
  kHz) do: check the edges and the 16-channel averaging (fine in B/C/D; in A a 195 kHz
  channel costs ~3% of the peak at 47' and ~18% at 150').
- Calibrator phases against time: ionospheric wraps on the long baselines, how far the
  phase calibrator is (1140+223 is 12.7 deg from NGC 4565 in AD0308), whether it is
  observed while the target is (the pipeline does not check), and whether the target,
  bright at 90 cm, should be its own phase calibrator (NED's check decides that today).
- 3C286 against Perley-Butler 2017 (~26.3 Jy at 327.5 MHz): fluxscale's transfer to the
  phase calibrator, against its catalogue P-band flux.
- Field-source fluxes against TGSS (150 MHz) and NVSS (1.4 GHz) interpolated, or the
  Texas survey at 365 MHz: the absolute scale and the primary-beam correction together.
- The primary-beam correction at the target's offset: CASA's model (131' FWHM at 327 MHz,
  zero past 156') gives 0.72 at 46.7' where a 150' beam gives 0.76, so fluxes there
  lean ~6% high (0.29 vs 0.41 at 85'); decide on a custom vptable (below) before
  trusting P-band fluxes beyond ~0.4 FWHM.
- Sidelobes of bright sources outside the imaged fields: the NVSS sources the plan lists
  as beyond the model (105 of them for AD0308, up to ~160 mJy apparent, each one a line
  in fit.json's field_warnings: cap or summarize them if P band stays), and the A-team
  far out (Vir A is 14 deg from IC 3599).
- Smearing: bandwidth (a 3.125 MHz channel costs ~4% of the peak at 47' in C config) and
  time (30 s records here), and w-projection's cost on a 4096-pixel field.
- A configuration (not isoplanatic): whether self-cal converges at all.

## Wide-field imaging: outlier fields beyond CASA's primary-beam model
Found 2026-10-07 on AB0596 (L band, D config, A2218). Kept here for a case that needs it.
- CASA's VLA primary-beam model (the Perley polynomial, EVLA Memo 195) is exactly zero
  beyond ~1.2 FWHM. tclean marks pixels there as invalid ("No valid values to
  deconvolve"), so an outlier field around a bright source 1.3 FWHM out (NVSS 437 mJy,
  ~7 mJy apparent, i.e. ~1.6% response measured) cannot be cleaned in the self-cal
  cycles; the initial automask clean got some of it, the cycle cleans none. Self-cal
  then stopped after one cycle (upper limit 2.6 vs 2.4 mJy without the outlier field).
- Option A (preferred if needed): a custom vptable, vpmanager.setpbairy for a 25 m dish
  with its blockage, maxrad 2-3 FWHM, and pblimit ~ -1e-6, so far fields have a nonzero
  response. Airy patterns are CASA's default for ALMA and dishes without a stored
  model; for the VLA it would be new. It also changes the main field's pb (the target's
  beam correction) by a few % inside half power: compare both before adopting.
- Option B: clean outlier fields only in the initial model, leave them out of cycles.
- Option C: fall back to the 2xFWHM main image when a bright source lies beyond
  ~1.2 FWHM (slow, L band only).
- Same limit applies to the TARGET: a far-field target beyond ~1.2 FWHM has no beam
  correction from CASA's model.
- The Gaussian beam the NVSS outlier prediction uses underestimates the skirt (0.8%
  vs 1.6% measured at 1.3 FWHM); PB_SIDELOBE_FLOOR is now 2% for that reason.

## Calibration
- Reference antenna: replace "3rd closest by vibes" (find_refant -> anntennas_list[3])
  with a principled central / low-flagging / present-the-whole-track pick, chosen once
  and fixed across cycles. (Array-config detection from antenna layout is done; refant
  selection itself is not.)
- fluxscale-failure retry: when fluxscale fails, try alternate refants with a
  checkpoint backup/restore of the data folder (from 1.99 refant retry loop).
- Manual flux calibration: setjy standard='manual' with user flux/freq, for odd/missing
  amplitude calibrators (Perley-Butler is the only path today).
- Missing flux calibrator, second rescue: search every project observed within ~24 h
  for scans of a standard flux calibrator at the right frequency, and pull those scans
  in (bootstrapping through a calibrator both observed). Better than today's rescue,
  which takes the phase calibrator's catalogue flux and is good to only ~10-20%.
- "Don't do self phase calibration" toggle.
- Solution bookkeeping: decide & document incremental vs non-incremental self-cal;
  implement check_refant (currently `pass`); optionally save per-cycle gain phase/amp
  plots + stats for archiving.

